  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8d1e7c28-9f24-4ac6-8d43-3ab1d2a80d01",
    "name": "Discord DMs \u2014 Lab 3",
    "description": "Requires the Discord REST permissions release. Use Gateway base_url=http://localhost:8090 and set token to a real login JWT, player_id to its subject and session_id to a dedicated test session. Start the session through Session Service, then set channel_id to one of its provisioned channels containing that player. Run Channels then Messages. Public channel creation/update/deletion must return 403; REST provisioning must return 410. Message operations create, edit and delete only this run's test message. Provisioned channels remain in place. Do not run these mutation checks against an older deployment. Discovery checks are optional: discovery_url is empty because CPR does not publish it. Supply an explicitly reachable address. Recovery checks need a manual Discovery restart between baseline/recovery requests. HTTP checks do not establish Socket.IO authentication, cross-replica delivery or complete authorization coverage. Do not commit tokens.",
